    {
      "id": "f9112a11fa1b06bfea47b4ca76d986018b6ec8f0",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402028385,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Please correct me if I'm wrong. This job runs a code quality check from gitlab on the whole source tree. It generates a json report that gets uploaded as artifact. To read the report I have to browse the artifacts, getting back a blob json (nearly unreadable). At least I'd suggest to pretty print the report on the screen instead of uploading as artifact. Once the report gets readable, we could move the discussion on the quality of the report itself.\n\n> Note: this may have issues with timing out. Those will need to be resolved prior to merging.\n\nCan you elaborate?",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-25T21:12:41.594Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-25T21:12:41.594Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 68601123,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c8124369d07ec63d83653707b86e02663921b76d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402037262,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It appears to have completed within 30 minutes, so it ran significantly faster than when I had tested it. It's possible Wireshark's licensing provides better performance.\n\nFrom the video embedded in the [GitLab docs](https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/user/project/merge_requests/code_quality.html), once the code quality job is added, future merge requests will display a code quality widget, which will present a readable report.",
          "author": {
            "id": 3194989,
            "username": "moshekaplan",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Moshe Kaplan",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/3194989/avatar.png?v=1789950604",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/moshekaplan"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-25T21:40:22.538Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-25T23:23:42.895Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 68601123,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bb5e91a4cf5232c0632cd03d175c4618c6849ffa",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402517117,
          "type": null,
          "body": "According to documentation, the checks are run by code climate, whose supported languages are\n\nhttps://docs.codeclimate.com/docs/supported-languages-for-maintainability\n\nThose include python and ruby (a marginal part of wireshark) but not C and C++ (> 93%). Then what's the advantage of adding code quality jobs?",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-26T14:26:40.082Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-26T14:26:40.082Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 68601123,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b95347a9a8256bfdee59fa1b488e3e6cf3ae5f4c",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402539089,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It appears that it supports basic checks for C/C++ code as well. Here's one random example:\n\n{\n\"categories\":[\"Bug Risk\"],\n\"check_name\":\"XXX\",\n\"description\":\"XXX found\",\n\"location\":{\"lines\":\"begin\":321,\"end\":321},\n\"path\":\"wiretap/peektagged.c\"},\n\"type\":\"issue\",\n\"engine_name\":\"fixme\",\n\"fingerprint\":\"629e074e950aac24d8aceb7204cf3779\",\n\"severity\":\n\"minor\"\n},\n\nLooking at that code, it's likely flagging on the \"XXX\":\nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/wiretap/peektagged.c#L321",
          "author": {
            "id": 3194989,
            "username": "moshekaplan",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Moshe Kaplan",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/3194989/avatar.png?v=1789950604",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/moshekaplan"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-26T14:56:10.360Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-26T14:56:10.360Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 68601123,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "eddf70f4858843bed095be07bd3b5832b42efb6c",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402550279,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I took the report and searched for \"epan/\". What I got is something like thousands of lines in the report complaining about comments like XXX, FIX, TODO and so on. A gigantic report of such is totally useless, unless the code gets cleaned first. Unless you want to try to fix the thousands of them, I'm downvoting this change.",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-26T15:10:37.876Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-26T15:10:37.876Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 68601123,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7e541b6d3395c1c510a994f055ce102876a70b47",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402556003,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The value isn't examining the report for all code, but specifically comparing the code quality **changes** with the widget:\n\nhttps://docs.gitlab.com/ee/user/project/merge_requests/code_quality.html#code-quality-widget\n\n![image](/uploads/46323737f9501ceccd05f2f7a07ed189/image.png)",
          "author": {
            "id": 3194989,
            "username": "moshekaplan",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Moshe Kaplan",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/3194989/avatar.png?v=1789950604",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/moshekaplan"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-26T15:19:00.525Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-26T15:19:00.525Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 68601123,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5bf2a530373d1b347491cb6cb03c26c195b4ec73",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402560833,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Still puzzled... I'm not really sure I want to add one more CI job based on a platform that doesn't list C as its supported languages. I would be glad to hear some more thoughts, like @pquantin's and @AndersBroman's.",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-26T15:24:50.959Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-26T15:24:50.959Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 68601123,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "95492155578931458e81cee27085d4e851b9208a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402593343,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi guys,\nnot convinced this will add a valuable information either. If we have too many reports / quality check performed, at the end I fear no one will look at them (too much information kills the information and the effort needed to go through all those reports will get higher).",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-26T16:10:08.695Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-26T16:10:08.695Z",
