    {
      "id": "c1c44eeff972a5cc0f6e65b870e93c11b3b26e05",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 403023678,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi,\nI'm doubtful too. But I think that the case Moshe is trying to make is that if we ignore the inital avalanche of \"faults\" we'll get an evaluation on single merge requests. Stil a bit doubtful though. It's alittle bit like the \"dead code\" checks where an offset +=1;\nas the last statment is beeing warned against and in my opinion actually casing bugs\nwhen you forgett to add it next itteration when new octets are to be decoded.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
